   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Generate the Synthetic Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The light-curve generator creates physically-motivated synthetic data for all 5 object classes. "
    "Each curve is 256 samples long (2 hours at 5-second cadence) with class-specific tumble dynamics, "
    "reflection models, and noise.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# Generate the dataset (2000 curves per class = 10,000 total)\n",
    "%%capture\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, '.')\n",
    "from src.pipeline.generate_dataset import main as generate_main\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will create data/synthetic/lightcurves.npz and splits\n",
    "generate_main()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Verify the dataset was created correctly\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# Load and inspect the dataset\n",
    "%%\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "data = np.load('data/synthetic/lightcurves.npz', allow_pickle=True)\n",
    "curves = data['curves']\n",
    "labels = data['labels']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Curves shape: {curves.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Labels shape: {labels.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unique classes: {np.unique(labels)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Class distribution: {dict(zip(*np.unique(labels, return_counts=True)))}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show one example per class\n",
    "class_names = ['Intact Satellite', 'Dead Satellite', 'Rocket Body', 'Fragmentation', 'Spoofed']\n",
    "for cls in range(5):\n",
    "    mask = labels == cls\n",
    "    example = curves[mask][0]\n",
    "    print(f\"{class_names[cls]}: min={example.min():.3f}, max={example.max():.3f}, mean={example.mean():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Extract Features from Light Curves\n",
    "\n",
    "We extract a combination of time-domain, frequency-domain, and temporal-pattern features "
    "that serve as input to both the quantum and classical models.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "source": [
    "# Extract features from a few curves\n",
    "%%\n",
    "from src.classical.feature_engineering import extract_all_features\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get first curve from each class\n",
    "data = np.load('data/synthetic/lightcurves.npz', allow_pickle=True)\n",
    "curves = data['curves']\n",
    "labels = data['labels']\n",
    "\n",
    "class_names = ['Intact Satellite', 'Dead Satellite', 'Rocket Body', 'Fragmentation', 'Spoofed']\n",
    "for cls in range(5):\n",
    "    mask = labels == cls\n",
    "    example = curves[mask][0]\n",
    "    feats = extract_all_features(example)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{class_names[cls]}:\")\n",
    "    for k, v in feats.items():\n",
    "        print(f\"  {k}: {v:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
